WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Great Drunken Kara-Age Debate</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.780
<b>Nobu</b>

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:36.140
Prosit!

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.650
Hermina-san, how is married life going?

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.290
It's going as expected.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.750
Is Berthold-san being kind to you?

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.360
It's going as expected.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.090
I'm worried because you're the quiet type.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.460
<b>Hermina (16)
Waitress at Nobu. Berthold's wife</b>

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:53.460
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of 
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.470
I mean, Berthold-san seems 
like he's rather stubborn.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.970
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company Commander of 
Aitheria Palace Guards aka "the Devil"</b>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:54.960
It's salt.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.200
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.210
No, it's soy sauce.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.310
They're still at it.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.890
No, salt.

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.620
Soy sauce is the only way.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.110
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.240
<i>Salt or soy sauce? This fruitless 
kara-age debate has been</i>

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.470
<i>raging between these two whenever they meet.</i>

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.110
<b>Fizz</b>

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.650
<b>Kara-age (Salt flavor)</b>

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.650
<b>If you think juicy fried chicken, 
salt flavor is the way to go</b>

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.640
Yeah, kara-age needs to be salt flavored.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.950
The balanced saltiness permeates 
all corners of my tired body.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.330
I'll let you have this one for today.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.740
<b>Kara-age (Soy sauce flavor)</b>

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:33.740
<b>If you think crunchy and delicious fried 
chicken, soy sauce flavor is the only way</b>

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.440
But today it's my turn.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.810
This aroma! Soy sauce really is 
the only true way to do kara-age!

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.220
<i>Until yesterday, they kept 
taking turns with the orders.</i>

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:51.440
<i>But maybe it's not their fault.</i>

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:54.280
<i>This may be the machinations 
of the devil called kara-age.</i>

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.690
<b>Fizz</b>

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:57.820
Thank you for waiting, 
here's your salt kara-age.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.070
Look at that kara-age's white skin.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.560
It's a pale beauty, just like Hermina.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.090
The world is captivated by salt kara-age.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.060
Here is your soy sauce kara-age.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.580
Apologies to Hermina-san,

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:17.450
but I prefer healthy beauties 
with darker wheat colored skin.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.910
There's nothing that can 
surpass soy sauce kara-age.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:25.540
Pale beauties and healthy beauties. 
I don't want to pass up either.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.930
Wait, why am even I talking about this?

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.040
It doesn't matter which one it is.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.580
That won't do!

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.580
That's not true!

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.770
Today's the day where we finally 
decide which is better.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.040
It really doesn't matter.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.260
But before we settle this...

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.270
Another whatsontap!

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.270
Another whatsontap!

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.190
That's already the third.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.350
Please think of me who has to keep 
up with you on an empty stomach.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:48.890
Then it's salt.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.700
No, soy sauce.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.920
Besides, Berthold-san, you 
seem to have forgotten,

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.710
but the first kara-age that 
had such a big impact on you

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.750
was undeniably soy sauce flavored!

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.930
Wha— That was so long ago!

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.530
And yet, now you're going on about salt.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.790
Nikolaus, you can wipe that superior 
"I'm the number one regular" look off your face.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.070
By now, I'm the kind of regular 
who comes to drink here

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.930
even by myself when you 
guys are too weak to come.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:24.210
That's because you force us to do ridiculous 
drills when you want to come here by yourself.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.920
That's nothing but false accusations.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.540
You're so transparent!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.210
As a company commander, I recommend salt.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:42.230
In order to draw out the maximum 
amount of umami that the ingredient,

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.740
the young chicken possesses, there 
is simply nothing better salt.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:49.950
The addition of garlic is also perfect for 
recovering your stamina after a day of training.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:53.620
Bringing your position into 
it is an abuse of power.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.050
It is imperative to ensure that 
the young chicken's umami

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.200
and the batter's flavor can become 
one for kara-age to attain

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:03.240
the highest possible value as a cooked dish.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.550
That's why soy sauce is 
the best flavor here.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:09.310
You sure talk big.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.210
If the original ingredient 
is so important to you,

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:14.290
just roast a bird and sprinkle salt on it.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.560
At this rate, I don't know when 
I can have some kara-age.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.270
Thank you for waiting.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.570
<b>Salt-Roasted Ginnan</b>

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.570
<b>One just can't stop eating these 
slightly bitter ginkgo nuts</b>

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.560
There they are!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:24.080
Oh, nice.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.490
What are these?

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:30.100
Salt-roasted ginnan. I ordered 
something else beforehand.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:33.170
Please crack the shell 
and eat the nut inside.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.430
Unlike edamame, it's bitter, and 
its unique aroma goes well with salt.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.060
So you finally realized how good salt is.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.700
So the kara-age should be salt as we—

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.330
I never said that!

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.340
<b>Maguro Sashimi</b>

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.340
<b>The shiny red meat of the 
tuna is a feast by itself.</b>

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.350
Here you go, your sashimi.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.850
What a gorgeous red.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.070
Well, let's have some.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:06.210
Yes, the soy sauce really 
enhances the umami.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:10.450
Which means that soy sauce 
is where it all begins.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.350
Enough already!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.400
I'm going to eat these!

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.080
That reminds me. You've been being 
annoying this whole time, Hans.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.560
Where do you stand then?

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.030
That's right. What is your 
choice, salt or soy sauce?!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.550
Me?

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.190
Right now it's 1-1 between 
salt and soy sauce.

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.660
If you add your vote, it'll settle it.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:35.540
That's a heavy burden, Hans. 
But you and I go way back.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:44.710
Huh? What? I'm the linchpin?

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.880
Now, Hans... of course it's salt, right?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.170
No, no, Berthold-san.

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:55.320
His face is twitching with the urge 
to come out as a soy sauce supporter.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.350
Don't force him like that.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.230
Hans should be choosing of his own volition.

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.530
By the way, Hans, about tomorrow's 
break during training...

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.130
Please stop it with your 
blatantly obvious bribery.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.400
Shi— Well, that was just a joke.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.840
No, what I heard was serious.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.610
Another order of salt kara-age please!

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:17.360
See, the world is for salt.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:19.870
Yeah, another order of 
soy sauce here please!

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.620
No, for soy sauce.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:25.140
Anyway, let's leave this to Hans.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.130
Which is it, Hans?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:31.260
Yeah, it's going to be easier 
if you just say it, Hans.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.510
What I like is—

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:35.950
What you like is?

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:36.870
Which is it?!

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.140
Tatsuta-age!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.390
Tatsuta-age, huh?

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:51.390
Tatsuta-age, is it?

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.790
Tatsuta-age is so delicious!

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.270
<i>This silence. It seems nobody 
can argue with that.</i>

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.040
The notable thing about 
tatsuta-age is its texture.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.680
He started a speech.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:08.560
I've never eaten another 
dish that pays that much

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.910
attention to the texture experience 
for your whole mouth.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:11.480
<b>Crunch</b>

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:16.770
That crunchy resistance as you bite 
tatsuta-age is truly a blessing.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:17.920
<b>Crunch</b>

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.890
<i>See, nobody could argue against that!</i>

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.820
Listen, Hans.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.420
Tatsuta-age...

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.970
isn't a type of kara-age.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:35.840
T-T-Tatsuta-age is similar enough though!

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:40.110
Give it up, Hans. Tatsuta-age and 
kara-age are two different dishes.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.530
Exactly.

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:45.520
Hm, I can't exactly confirm that.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:46.370
Huh?

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:48.080
What do you mean, Taishou?

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:54.240
Simply said, kara-age uses flour, 
while tatsuta-age uses potato starch.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:59.860
<b>Flour</b>

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:59.860
<b>Potato starch</b>

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.640
But lately, potato starch is 
used quite often for kara-age

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.680
as well to give it more crunchiness.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.090
In particular, soy sauce kara-age and 
tatsuta-age are pretty similar.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.360
I can't believe it.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.600
Th-That's right, Taishou! 
That's what I was trying to say!

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.810
He so didn't know that.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.090
Definitely not.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.100
Here you go, soy sauce kara-age.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:17.110
Here is your salt kara-age.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:20.950
Soy sauce kara-age and 
tatsuta-age are similar.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:28.140
I get it now, Hans! You said tatsuta-age, but 
you're really a secret ally for soy sauce!

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:28.950
Huh?

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.540
I knew you'd pick friendship!

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.420
Now it's 2-1 for soy sauce!

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:35.870
The kara-age we're getting 
is soy sauce flavored!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.910
No way! That's not...

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:39.670
Hermina! You prefer salt, right?!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.580
I already told Taishou what your order is.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.940
<b>Sizzle sizzle sizzle</b>

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:54.480
<b>Sizzle sizzle sizzle</b>

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.960
That's the sound of double-frying.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.740
Taishou's already making some kara-age.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.600
Which one will it be?

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:57.480
Here you go. This is for you.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.480
<b>Cartilage Kara-age</b>

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.480
<b>This crispy cartilage kara-age 
goes excellently with beer!</b>

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.990
H-Hermina-san? What is this?

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:03.800
The kara-age you ordered, dear.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.750
Both salt and soy sauce flavored.

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.970
But this is cartilage kara-age. 
It's tasty, too, but...

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:13.610
Today's kara-age is already sold out.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.960
Come on, Taishou, you could 
have said something.

00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:21.110
I'm sorry, I tried to say something, but...

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.080
I stopped him.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:24.350
Huh?

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:36.060
We can't refuse other customers' 
orders just because

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.830
you're having a nonsensical 
debate instead of ordering.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:43.040
Anyway, dear, eat up now.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:51.780
Nikolaus, Hans, let's get to eating already.

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:56.230
This is not the time to inconvenience the 
people of this place with our silly debate.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:00.030
The good cartilage kara-age 
is going to get cold.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.850
I never knew.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.180
You're so right.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.450
Berthold-san is completely under her heel.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.610
Let's eat!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.890
You're definitely right.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.760
Ah, so good.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.410
Yes, you're right. Both salt and soy sauce.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.030
Yes. Cartilage kara-age is the best!

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:41.990
<b>Ebisu</b>

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.860
We've come to Ebisu.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.230
When I asked if it's in the drinking 
part of town, I was told "no."

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:41.990
You'll be surprised.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.530
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:46.540
A place for kara-age. A place that 
could start a kara-age debate.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.250
Look forward to the three types of kara-age.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:53.760
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.640
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:55.340
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu."

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:56.250
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:01.010
We've wandered quite far from 
the drinking part of town.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:02.990
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi</b>

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.510
It's a bit hidden.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.520
Wasn't there something
 about umbrellas?

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:04.390
The umbrellas are the sign!

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.910
<b>Ebisu

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:04.940
These!

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:05.750
Correct!

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.010
Where do you get in?

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:08.480
Isn't it like a hideout?

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.190
Ah, from here. Yes.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:11.450
Sumibi Dojo Bettei is a 
serious place specializing in

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:13.200
<b>Sumibi Dojo Bettei</b>

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:13.220
poultry dishes that uses 
high-grade charcoal.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:14.200
Welcome.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:19.580
Ah, hello. Someone whispered in my ear that 
you have three types of kara-age here.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:19.570
<b>Bettei
CEO Kenji Sugou-san</b>

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.010
Yes.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:20.720
Yes, leave it to us.

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:21.950
This is a really nice place.

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.680
Isn't it though?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:22.680
Thank you.

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:23.520
How long has it been open?

00:11:23.520 --> 00:11:25.610
This is the ninth year.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.000
Really? It's so nice.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.810
While you're looking around, 
the prep work got finished.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:32.900
Enjoy a whatsontap
while they're frying.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.890
Oh, this sound!
 It's too much!

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:35.900
What might this be?

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.780
<b>Kara-age</b>

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:37.450
It's kara-age.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.600
Well, they all look like kara-age.

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:42.590
So what's this
place's specialty?

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:44.870
All our marinades are 
made by hand here.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.360
What kind of chicken do you use?

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.560
This is a chicken called
Daisen Takumidori.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.470
Those are chickens from 
Tottori Prefecture's Daisen.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.090
I'll try these.

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:54.200
Daisen chicken is known for 
its juiciness. How is it?

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.750
The flavor is really in there. 
What are these on the side here?

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:00.270
That is our tatsuta-age.

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.500
<b>Tatsuta-age</b>

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:01.680
I'll try this tatsuta-age.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.040
How is the tatsuta-age?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.030
Yep, this is good too!

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.240
And the one that my eyes 
keep going to is this one.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.740
<b>Chicken Nanban</b>

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.740
That's the Miyazaki 
specialty, chicken nanban.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:19.210
Please try it as is first, then please 
try some with the tartar sauce.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:14.790
All right.

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.300
Once I've tasted it, I should 
use the tartar sauce.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:23.750
Yes.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:27.330
The tartar sauce just
goes so well with it!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:32.620
There's soy sauce and vinegar on this. 
This nanban thing, it's delicious.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:36.520
When you add the tartar sauce, the 
flavor changes quite a bit and...

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:39.790
makes it really tasty.

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:41.490
Are these Iburi pickles?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:42.300
No, they are not!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.350
Those are sweet potato fries.

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:48.840
Sweet potato? That's kind of unusual.
These are really sweet. What's your secret?

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:52.880
Those are our company's own potatoes, 
the "Hinatamitsu potato."

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:56.140
Just by letting them ripen and cooking 
them at a controlled temperature,

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:59.090
<b>Hinatamitsu Potato
 Reach a sugar content of 70 Brix
 just by taking fully ripened
 potatoes and cooking them while
controlling the temperature.</b>

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:58.080
they reach a sugar
 content of about 70 Brix.

00:12:58.080 --> 00:13:01.300
Seventy?! Lately my sugar 
content's quite high, too.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.650
Nobody wants to know that.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:03.680
Not that it's any good.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:04.700
Seriously.

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.390
What do you really recommend though?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.960
That would be
the chicken nanban.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:12.840
I agree. I liked that the 
best. It's just good.

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.700
And these sweet 
potato Iburi pickles?

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:15.610
That wasn't funny
 the first time!

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.960
Why do they go so well together?

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:19.900
Oh no, this goes with that, too.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:21.070
Of course it does.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.700
But you knew that.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:25.680
Even Nagira-san approves 
of "Sumibi Dojo Bettei."

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.490
It's a five minute walk 
from the Ebisu Station.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.090
